{
 "comment": "Template for a new Playden language. Copy this file to assets/translations/<code>.json, fill in code and name, translate the values and add the code and name to assets/translations/index.json. This template is not a catalogue and never ships: only the files index.json lists are packaged. Keys are the English strings exactly as the source writes them and must not be edited. A value left empty keeps that string in English, so a partial catalogue is fine, and a name that should not change (Playden, Steam, Windows) is best left empty. Legends name a controller button first (Cross, Circle, Square, Triangle, Options, Touchpad, L1/R1): keep that prefix in English, it picks the glyph and is dropped before the words are drawn. Only glyphs the font atlas carries can be drawn: printable ASCII, Latin-1 Supplement, Latin Extended-A, Greek, Cyrillic and a few marks.",
